text=['# MobiPEG Web Studio — implementation and validation','', 'Date: November 16, 2026. Status: functional release preview; physical iPhone Safari and Nintendo hardware remain unverified.','', 'The actual supplied V15 layout-0 fixed FFmpeg/x264 source was compiled with Emscripten 4.0.10. Both a scalar codec and a SIMD codec are included. The browser runs the native FFmpeg scheduler using pthreads while the codec itself uses one thread. FFprobe independently identifies output as `mobiclip` video and `adpcm_ima_moflex` audio. No stock ffmpeg.wasm codec was substituted.','', '## Measured native / WASM comparisons','', 'These full-file measurements use the browser WASM binary under Node, compared against a rebuilt native V15 core using the same settings. WASM totals include process/module startup and verification. The browser reuses a compiled module within a conversion, so these Node totals are not direct iPhone/Chrome speed predictions. Some timing runs overlapped build/test activity; treat speeds as indicative, not controlled performance measurements.','', '| Input | Native bytes | WASM bytes | Coded frames | Native PSNR | WASM PSNR | Native SSIM | WASM SSIM | Native time | WASM time |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in rows:
 if r['name'] not in ['yip-full','anime-full','avatar-full-3d']:continue
 a,b=r['native'],r['wasm'];an=r['analysis'];text.append(f"| {r['name']} | {a['bytes']:,} | {b['bytes']:,} | {b['frames']:,} | {an['native']['psnr']} | {an['wasm']['psnr']} | {an['native']['ssim']} | {an['wasm']['ssim']} | {elapsed(a['elapsedSeconds'])} | {elapsed(b['elapsedSeconds'])} |")
text += ['', 'PSNR is FFmpeg all-plane average PSNR against the aligned, resized/rate-converted source, not the previous project reports’ luma-only PSNR. SSIM is FFmpeg All. Resolution is 400×224; full Avatar is half-SBS → layout-0 stereo. These results are not Nintendo quality comparisons.','', 'See the table for the final corrected measurements. Full Anime differs by +4,096 bytes (about +0.031%) and −0.000418 dB PSNR. The Avatar row is now the SAR-corrected, full-width 3D pipeline, and cannot be compared directly to the old narrow/pillarboxed result. Their decoded pixels are not completely identical to native. The precise cause of these small long-form codec differences has not been established. A separate three-second raw preprocessing comparison is byte-identical. Do not claim universal byte identity.','', 'The final full Avatar uses the SIMD engine. Its corrected native output was reused and reverified; native timing is not available for that final run. No new byte-identity guarantee is implied by the small mean quality deltas.', '', '## Checks actually executed','', '- 249 controller/unit checks passed, including 180 filter-graph combinations compared directly with Python V15. Mocked failure-path tests are controller tests, not codec runs.','- Original Studio suite: 11 passed and 4 skipped because the exact named fixtures were absent. Synthetic real stereo/audio integration ran successfully.','- The initial 19 paired scenarios were supplemented by corrected half-SBS reruns and a proper half-SBS geometry fixture. The current main dataset contains 13 scenarios, with 3 additional SIMD short cases, full SIMD Anime, a 10-minute SIMD sample, a padded 128 MiB input, and the proper half-SBS geometry case. Earlier pre-SAR reports are retained under reports/history and are not current geometry validation. Candidate size trials add extra real encodes beyond the finished-pair count.','- All 13 main cases passed full video/audio decode, packet/frame checks, native/WASM PSNR tolerance of 0.01 dB and SSIM tolerance of 0.0001. All decoded audio PCM hashes match.','- All quality presets, five supported frame rates, three resolutions, all four filters and on/off/auto motion control appear in the real conversion matrix. Controller graph checks cover all mode/rate/resolution/filter combinations; this is not an exhaustive real-encode cross-product.','- Real maximum-size search completed six candidates and enforced the actual completed MOFLEX size. Corrupt input and an impossible 4,096-byte audio/video budget were rejected by the real WASM pipeline.','- Raw MOFLEX descriptors verify layout 0 stereo, per-eye dimensions and display FPS. Red-left/blue-right decoded pixels verify eye ordering at integer and fractional rates.','- 18 full-file seek checks returned pixel-identical frames to linear decoding at matching requested times. These are FFmpeg seek tests, not Nintendo player tests.','- Scene-cut scan found 74 Anime and 24 Avatar cuts at a 0.35 detection threshold. The regenerated reports/scene-cuts.json records final near-cut quality differences; the detector is applied to both complete source videos. Detection is heuristic, not a canonical edit list.','- Main-case audio duration padding error is at most about 4.3 ms and is identical to native. There is no introduced aggregate audio-duration drift in these samples. This is not perceptual lip-sync certification.','- Chrome UI: actual full-SBS and half-SBS conversions completed, downloaded files matched the original Python V15 outputs byte-for-byte, and cancellation restored controls.','', '## Long file / memory / SIMD results','', '| Test | Result |','|---|---|', f"| 10-minute 320×240 low-complexity sample | {simd[1]['wasm']['frames']:,} frames; {simd[1]['wasm']['bytes']:,} bytes; byte-identical to native; {simd[1]['wasm']['elapsedSeconds']:.2f}s WASM total |",'| Large-file fixture | 128 MiB MP4 created by padding a 1-second clip; byte-identical output. Tests large-file handling, not large-movie complexity or mobile memory. |','| Main full-file WASM heaps | See reports/benchmarks.json for measured heaps, including the updated full-width Avatar rerun. These are linear-memory heaps per command, not total process/tab memory. |',f"| Full Anime SIMD | {simd[0]['wasm']['elapsedSeconds']:.2f}s total, versus 121.24s scalar in these indicative runs; SIMD output is byte-identical to scalar WASM. |", '| SIMD short cases | All three match native exactly. SIMD source motion-search loops were auto-vectorized; the scalar core remains available as Compatibility. |','', 'The original muxer retains the movie payload and pending packets to build its front seek table. WORKERFS removes the need to copy the entire original input into the browser filesystem, but does not remove muxer buffers, decoded frames, output blobs or overlapping WASM heaps. Arbitrary feature-length/high-bitrate movies are not certified. A disk-backed muxer remains future work.','', '## Important fixes found during the port','', '1. Adapted x264 platform detection for the Emscripten cross-build and configured the custom x264 pkg-config path.','2. Built FFmpeg’s actual unstripped JS/WASM link target instead of passing its JS loader through native strip; renamed the WASM reference consistently.','3. Exported runtime filesystem/environment/heap/thread support and supplied the correct pthread loader URL.','4. Applied MOBI settings in preRun, before C environment initialization. Applying them after module readiness silently left some native defaults in use; the real comparison tests detected this and all final results were rerun after the fix.','5. Isolated every CLI command in a fresh WASM instance to prevent static FFmpeg/x264 settings leaking between jobs.','6. Added mandatory COOP/COEP hosting and a static-host service-worker isolation fallback. Direct local-server headers were exercised in Chrome; fallback behavior is browser-dependent.','7. Added SIMD plus scalar fallback without changing codec syntax or adopting quality-reducing shortcuts.','', '8. Corrected inherited half-SBS fitting by adding scale reset_sar=1 when the eye SAR is 2. Confirmed near-corner colors on a proper half-SBS fixture and reran the full trailer.', '', '## Unverified / incomplete','', '- No physical iPhone Safari, Firefox, WebKit, Old3DS or New3DS run was available. The optional Playwright suite/config is included but was not executed; WebKit emulation would not equal a real iPhone test.','- No multi-hour high-complexity video, exhaustive supported-input-codec matrix, tab-total-memory measurement or long background/suspend recovery test.','- No pause/resume, disk-backed muxing or recovery from a closed/crashed tab. The site is responsive by implementation; a physical mobile viewport/device QA pass remains pending.','- Sample-specific offline optimization/research scripts remain in the full source package; they are not presented as new browser controls. Standard Studio V15 functionality is ported.','', '## Reproduction and evidence','', 'See README.md, scripts/build-wasm.sh, scripts/build-simd.sh and tests/. Machine-readable reports, source hashes, per-frame PSNR/SSIM, seek hashes, browser results and aligned image comparisons accompany this report. Source media is not redistributed inside the source archive. Optional external browser tests require @playwright/test and local fixtures.','']
